 "findings": [
  "Prefix caching reproduces the merge screening rows on this host: MoE 35B all lanes goes 28.19 -> 33.88 tok/s (-16.8% wall) with 16/27 hits and 42,496 reused tokens against the screening run's 28.15 -> 33.48 at the same turn and token counts, and dense 27B code lanes goes 5.64 -> 7.35 tok/s (-23.3% wall) with 9/18 hits, 39,168 reused tokens and median prefill 6,362 -> 2,953 ms.",
  "Served per-request decode rate at c=1 with cache off: rows that used MTP decode at 25.34 tok/s against the in-load true-AR control's 12.27 (2.07x), with median ITL 40.1 against 82.8 ms. The matched per-turn comparison favours the speculative arm at every turn (turn medians 12.4/28.6, 12.3/24.6, 12.2/25.4, 12.1/16.1 tok/s for control/speculative).",
  "That is a per-request result, not an aggregate throughput claim. This load is deliberately mixed-route, so its wall rate (12.34 tok/s over 16 requests, 165.9 s) is a property of the load and not of either arm, and no all-MTP-versus-all-AR pair was run here.",
  "At c=4 the per-request advantage is gone: MTP rows decode at 9.59 against the AR arm's 9.30 tok/s (1.03x) with ITL 108.9 against 110.2 ms, while the load aggregate rises to 21.65 tok/s. Concurrency buys the aggregate and the route adds nothing per request on this load. This is a measurement, not an attribution: the split is task #31's subject.",
  "Field trap recorded so it is not repeated: the harness's per-arm `decode_tokens_per_second` divides the group's tokens by its longest request duration (`wall = max(e2e_ms)`), so with per-conversation arm assignment, where both arms' rows are spread across the whole load, it reports nearly identical values for both arms (76.50 against 74.84) and cannot compare them. `by_route_arm` does not publish a per-request rate at all; it must be derived from the rows, and `median_itl_ms` is the arm-level latency the harness does publish. A first pass of this baseline reported the span-based field as a throughput-parity result and is retracted here.",
  "Warm prefix hits do not use MTP: on the radix server at c=1 only 2 of 8 speculative-arm rows engage and both are cache misses, while all six hit rows refuse with no_provider; at c=4 no hit row engages. Those two engaged rows decode at 28.46 against the AR arm's 12.21 tok/s per request.",
  "The c=4 speculative lane loses coverage to activation, not to group width: 2 of 6 rows engage with 635 no_provider events, and every realized group in all five loads is one row (groups_by_realized_rows has a single key, \"1\").",
  "Served diagnostics are populated on the merged tree: fallback_reason, effective_route, policy_reason, k0_class and mtp_used all carry values on the speculative arm, where pre-merge rows reported nulls, and the only non-MTP reason on the AR-control arm is the harness's own unknown (a request that never carried speculative intent).",
  "Prefix caching does not cost hit latency here: radix c=1 median TTFT is 1,271 ms overall (hits 1,327, misses 1,152) and at c=4 hits reach first token faster than misses (6,178 against 9,252 ms median).",
  "The cancellation load completes safely: 10 requests, 2 cancelled after their first tokens, 0 failures, with MTP active in the same load.",
  "The radix server reports 17 hipengine_kv_pool_grow_failures_total with 0 grow events and no request failures, so the merged allocator's retry path is exercised on this load; the off arm reports 0."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "One timing run per arm, sequential arm order, no repetition: this is a working baseline, not admission evidence, and day-to-day host drift is not bounded by it.",
  "The served numbers come from one server process per cache mode and one seed (4242); the c=4 loads use three turns rather than four, so they are not turn-for-turn comparable with the c=1 loads.",
  "Throughput is compared only within this protocol. The historical natural-short lane (median 36-token prompts) and the external porting record's 517/945-token shapes are different workloads and are not comparable to these rates.",
  "No rocprofv3 cycle attribution, no per-phase host/device split, and no candidate-budget sweep were run; that is task #31 and its absence is why the current gap split remains unmeasured.",
  "MTP acceptance here is the server's own aggregate (0.602 cache-off, 0.672 radix) over a small load, not the category suite.",
  "No production numerical qualification is claimed: the dense27B serial-oracle divergence recorded in the merge qualification artifact is unresolved."
 ]
}
